# Every text file is LF in the index and in every checkout, on every platform. Goldens, testdata,
# go:embed'd files, scripts, hooks and the capcom register are all read byte-for-byte, and a
# core.autocrlf=true checkout (Windows CI) would otherwise put a carriage return on each line —
# a golden then diffs while printing identically, and //go:embed bakes the \r into the binary.
# One default covers every path, so a new byte-compared path needs no pin of its own.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files are run by cmd.exe, which wants CRLF: the index copy stays LF and the
# conversion happens on checkout only.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary fixtures and assets are never converted: a CRLF byte pair inside a PDF, an image or a
# font would be rewritten on `git add` and corrupt the file.
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.ttf binary
*.ico binary

# Issue files merge through the capcom-log driver, defined in each operator's global git config.
.capcom/issues/**/*.md merge=capcom-log
